Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||05-14-2001||04:23 PM||||I am an engineer and believe me when I tell you - if they were there when the car was made, or esp if they were put on in a recall, it is because they are NECESSARY!!!<P>  Big manufacturing companies (like Pontiac) dont put stuff on cars that doesnt need to be there - every dollar here and 5 bucks there adds up to big money when you are making 100,000 cars a year.||||reg||1
Z||000004||moonie||05-14-2001||05:19 PM||||heres the gig , <BR>after reading replies i called engine install<BR>shop (American Engine Installation ), i 'splained to them that i am now missing that heat shield. they supposedly called pontiac & they told them that its no longer required.<BR>i may be describing it wrong , its the aluminum piece that goes between the exhaust manifold & the head. it kinda stuck straight up with flanges on the sides & top. <BR>anyway , they 'splained that the new gasket material makes that obsolete.<BR>and , with a 36,000 mile/ 3yr warranty , i guess its on them if something happens.<BR>thank you very much for your advice.<BR>moonster <P>||||reg||1
